/code-review high — loop U5, round 1, range 30b9e8f..0f9c230

1. tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin:69 — The new `canBeResolved && !canBeConsumed` filter skips every configuration a user creates with `configurations.creating`/`create()`. In Gradle 8 these are both resolvable and consumable by default (e.g. `val ktlint by configurations.creating`, `detekt`, custom tool configs), so their locks are no longer checked or written.
   Failure: a project with `dependencyLocking { lockAllConfigurations() }` and `val ktlint by configurations.creating` gets a dynamic `ktlint` version bump. The normal run never resolves `ktlint` under STRICT and passes. `--upgrade` runs `--write-locks` with the same filter, so the `ktlint` entry is never written or refreshed. The old task resolved every `canBeResolved` configuration and caught this.
2. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/android:55 — A file at the Gradle root now maps to `.` (the root project only) instead of `all`. In a multi-module build the root project has no lint task, so a change to the root `build.gradle(.kts)`, root `lint.xml` or root `lint-baseline.xml` lints nothing.
   Failure: a commit edits only the root `build.gradle.kts` or the root `lint.xml`. MODULES_ARG becomes `.`, the init script picks the root project, which has no `lint` task. `bootstrapLint` has no dependencies and succeeds, so lint is silently skipped. The old code linted every module.
3. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android:158 — The "installed `_ps16k` variant counts as the image" shortcut applies at every API level and even to an explicit `EMULATOR_IMAGE`. The requested 4 KB-page image is silently swapped for the 16 KB variant and never installed.
   Failure: `EMULATOR_IMAGE=system-images/android-35/google_apis/arm64-v8a`, `google_apis_ps16k/arm64-v8a` installed, plain image absent → the task uses the variant and installs nothing. Before, the variant was used only when the SDK list lacked the requested image.
4. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android:203 — The new post-install check turns every mismatch between `installed()` (`${ANDROID_HOME:-}/<id>/package.xml`) and where `android sdk install` writes into a hard failure. The task never checks that ANDROID_HOME is set.
   Failure: ANDROID_HOME unset or different from the CLI's SDK root → install succeeds but every package is reported as not installed and setup exits 1 on each run. Before, the mismatch only caused a redundant reinstall.
5. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android:37 — The AGP detect in build-logic/ narrowed from any file to `*.kts|*.kt|*.gradle|*.toml`. Java and Groovy convention-plugin classes that apply `com.android.application` are no longer seen.
   Failure: the only `com.android.application` reference is `build-logic/convention/src/main/groovy/AndroidAppPlugin.groovy` (or `.java`) → no AGP found, the task exits 0 silently. The old `grep -r build-logic` found it.
6. tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin:113 — Removed invariant: the normal run no longer checks that the lockfiles on disk match git, and drops the "needs a git repository" error, so outside git it prints a false "No project has dependencyLocking" warning.
   Failure: a developer runs `--upgrade` and does not commit; the normal run passes against the modified lockfiles. In a non-git checkout `lockfiles` fails, LOCKS is empty, and the task warns that no project has locking.
7. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android:51 — The applicability detect depends on `git ls-files` with errors sent to /dev/null; when git cannot list the files, the task silently does not apply.
   Failure: not a git work tree, `safe.directory` refusal, or Android modules in a nested submodule → exit 0 with no output, no SDK packages installed. The old `find` detect worked.
8. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android:31 — Efficiency: the loop stats and case-matches every tracked and untracked file under bash 3.2. Pass pathspecs to git (`-- '*.gradle' '*.gradle.kts' 'build-logic/*' 'gradle/libs.versions.toml'`) as `lockfiles()` in the kotlin task does.
9. tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/android:49 — `module_of` finds a module only by `build.gradle(.kts)`. A remapped project with a custom `buildFileName` (e.g. `app.gradle.kts`) falls to `.` (root only) instead of "no project → lint every module".
   Failure: `project(":app").buildFileName = "app.gradle.kts"`; a change in `app/src/...` maps to `.`, the root project exists, nothing is linted.
